{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity review of the entire patent application draft, including all claims, the detailed description, the numerals, the abstract, and all figure briefs. I traced every technical feature and limitation back to the affirmative inventor disclosure in `input/disclosure.md` and `input/conversation.md`. I also checked for internal consistency across all parts of the application.\n\nThe review found two instances where the figure briefs introduce specific geometric or functional details that are not supported by the inventor's disclosure. These details go beyond allowable depiction conventions for schematic drawings because they define specific functional shapes and operating characteristics that the inventor did not describe. The first finding concerns an unsupported description of the cross-sectional shape of the rigid spacer frame. The second finding concerns an unsupported characterization of the visibility of the mechanical indicator stem. Both require correction to ensure the application is fully supported by the source disclosure.\n\nI have prepared detailed findings for each issue, including the location, evidence from the source, and a precise, ready-to-implement fix to bring the text into compliance."}
